# TEMPORAL.plan — per-run temporal capture map (copy to runs/$RID/TEMPORAL.plan)
#
# One `phase=T` line per frame to capture. T is a value in the APP'S OWN time
# units (seconds, frames, or whatever its --at seek accepts), OBSERVED from a dry
# run of the subject's app — never invented, never guessed. capture_temporal.sh
# renders each phase at 120x40 color and 120x40 Mono.
#
# Fill this in ONLY after watching the app run. If the app has no seekable
# timeline / no temporal transition, delete every line below and write exactly:
#     NONE
# (then only the static capture.sh ladder applies to this run).
#
# The seven canonical phases of a directed transition. Keep only the ones the
# app actually has; a piece may not reach every phase.
establish=
pre-transition=
transition-midpoint=
post-transition=
reveal=
hold=
payoff=
#
# When the app has a sharp transition at a boundary b, ALSO bracket it so the
# review can see the transition read as a transform rather than a cut. Set b to
# the observed boundary time and eps to a small step in the app's units; the
# three times are b-eps, b, b+eps.
transition_pre=
transition=
transition_post=
